# =============================================================================
# HomeWorld commit template
# =============================================================================
# ONE developer, SEVERAL agents. Your review attention is the scarcest resource in
# the company, so this asks for the one thing that makes a diff cheap to review:
# what the agent INVENTED, stated up front rather than discovered on read.
#
# Delete any section that genuinely does not apply. An unfilled template that
# says "N/A" everywhere is worse than no template, because it trains you to skip it.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ASSUMPTIONS  <- the section that matters. Fill it in or delete it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What did you decide that I did not tell you?
#
# Anything you chose between two defensible options. Anything you could not verify
# and proceeded anyway. Anything that touches art, game feel, mechanics, palette,
# silhouette, or scope - those are MINE, not yours (see docs/human-use/OWNERSHIP.md
# and docs/human-use/cursor-cannot/). If you had to make one to finish, say so here
# so I can reverse it in one minute instead of finding it in the diff.
#
# Assumed:
# -
# Could not verify:
# -

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERIFIED  <- what did you actually run?
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not "tests pass". Name the command and the result.
#
# Verified:
# - <command> -> <result>
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT DONE  <- what did you deliberately skip?
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The most valuable line in this template. An agent that reports its omissions is
# safe to supervise; one that silently drops half the task is not.
#
# Not done:
# -

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits: feat / fix / docs / test / refactor / chore / perf
# Scope when it helps. Body explains WHY, not what - the diff already says what.
# =============================================================================